/* Deep lessons — Computational geometry (geometry).
 *
 * Geometry has a reputation in competitive programming for being the section
 * where correct ideas still get wrong answers. That is because the ideas are
 * usually easy and the ARITHMETIC is not: a comparison with eps in the wrong
 * place, a double where a long long belonged, a degenerate case nobody drew.
 *
 * So this track builds everything out of two primitives — the dot product and
 * the cross product — keeps to integers wherever integers are possible, and
 * spends a whole late stage on precision, because that is what actually
 * decides whether a geometry solution passes.
 *
 * Original text and diagrams. Nothing copied from any source.
 */

import type { DeepLesson } from "../deep-lesson";

